      "side": 1,
      "message": "As described in the comments, getVpnIsolationInterface is our primary changed function -- it now considers lockdown status -- but it is only actually called from two functions, both within ConnectivityService (not here in PermissionMonitor): updateVpnUids and updateVpnFiltering. Neither of these is triggered in any way by this call to updateVpnUid within PermissionMonitor, so this shouldn\u0027t work. One place that might work is handleSetRequireVpnForUids, but in order to utilize existing functions, we must be able to reliably track previous and current lockdown state, because onVpnUidRangesRemoved and onVpnUidRangesAdded need to know the old and new isolation interface. See other comment.\n\nAnyway, I am still not sure how this patch overall *ever* works when toggling lockdown, but it does appear to work sometimes.",
